            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic pain: an undescribed paroxysmal manifestation of multiple sclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient with pelvic pain as a paroxysmal manifestation of multiple sclerosis (MS). This phenomenon has not been described previously; it can lead to diagnostic difficulties. Like other paroxysmal manifestations, it showed a good response to carbamazepine. The literature on paroxysmal manifestations of MS and some possible pathogenic mechanisms are reviewed briefly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
